1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,542
19–18. A real NBA final score.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,850
In 1950, there was no shot clock.

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:10,331
A team could hold the ball forever.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,426
Fort Wayne faced George Mikan's Lakers, and just held it.

5
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,653
Mikan still scored 15 of their 18.

6
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,894
Then, in the last seconds…

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,800
And Fort Wayne won it.

8
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:26,550
Four years later: the 24-second shot clock.

9
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,905
Still the lowest-scoring game in NBA history.
